.TH SDL_HINT_FILE_DIALOG_DRIVER 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_FILE_DIALOG_DRIVER \- A variable that specifies a dialog backend to use.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_FILE_DIALOG_DRIVER \(dqSDL_FILE_DIALOG_DRIVER\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
By default, SDL will try all available dialog backends in a reasonable order until it finds one that can work, but this hint allows the app or user to force a specific target\[char46]
.PP
If the specified target does not exist or is not available, the dialog-related function calls will fail\[char46]
.PP
This hint currently only applies to platforms using the generic \(dqUnix\(dq dialog implementation, but may be extended to more platforms in the future\[char46] Note that some Unix and Unix-like platforms have their own implementation, such as macOS and Haiku\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu NULL: Select automatically (default, all platforms)
.PP
\(bu \(dqportal\(dq: Use XDG Portals through DBus (Unix only)
.PP
\(bu \(dqzenity\(dq: Use the Zenity program (Unix only)
.PP
More options may be added in the future\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

